**Date:** 30 October 2026 · **Author:** Swiatlomost with AI harness.

## Context

The subject-only rule in [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merged
different mechanisms into #4471. It also separates identical causes described with different words.
The current runnable DedupeExplorer and CauseTable disagree with the old prose.

## Decision

This record supersedes 0001 for current triage. Preserve 0001 unedited as an audit trail.
Merge only after establishing the same cause in the relevant tenant configuration and channel.
For this export, use causeOf and sameCause in src/lib/kb/causes.ts with tenantOf in locales.ts.
A matching subject is a search clue, not proof. Unknown tenants or uncertain mechanisms stay separate
pending investigation; two unknown causes do not make a duplicate.

<DedupeExplorer />

## Consequences

Investigating configuration costs more than matching titles, but avoids hiding an unfixed issue.
Keep one issue per demonstrated mechanism, count unique report IDs and retain exact anomalies.
Reassess the classifier against new evidence rather than treating it as infallible.
Review the triage guide with each incident; a page over the layout's stale threshold needs rechecking.
This desk record is a submitted recommendation, not a claim of real-world staff approval.

